Packwood had gone through a divorce in 1991, and his ex-wife threatened to run against him amid mounting concerns about his "eye for the ladies." The socially conservative [[Oregon Citizens Alliance]] (OCA) was at the apex of its statewide prominence with 1992's anti-gay [[Oregon Ballot Measure 9 (1992)|Measure 9]] and its newly formed American Heritage Party (AHP). The group endorsed Republican challenger Joe Lutz, who had run against Packwood in the past on a [[family values]] platform; but Lutz soon withdrew, announcing a divorce of his own. As early as January, the OCA considered backing former gubernatorial candidate [[Al Mobley]] as an [[independent (politician)|independent]] or as a member of the AHP.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mapes |first=Jeff |date=January 16, 1992 |title=Mobley, OCA consider independent Senate race |work=The Oregonian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Sarasohn |first=David |author-link=David Sarasohn |date=July 26, 1992 |title=OCA party needs more normal name |work=The Oregonian}}</ref> Mobley ultimately decided in mid-August not to run, stating that he could not bear the idea that he might be responsible for causing AuCoin to be elected.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Schwartz |first1=Maralee |last2=Thomas B. Edsall |date=August 16, 1992 |title=Big break for Sen. Packwood |newspaper=The Washington Post}}</ref> Packwood's most significant challenge thus came from little-known conservative [[Medford, Oregon|Medford]] attorney John DeZell, who campaigned on the family values issue.<ref name="burke">{{Cite news |last=Wolf |first=Richard |date=December 3, 1992 |title=Capitol to Cabinet: Some potential picks |work=USA Today |url=https://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/USAToday/access/56243132.html?dids=56243132:56243132&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT%3A |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121023081639/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/USAToday/access/56243132.html?dids=56243132:56243132&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT: |url-status=dead |archive-date=October 23, 2012 |access-date=April 2, 2010}}</ref> Packwood cruised to victory over DeZell and several other candidates.

